{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LfYX4Yf8QVeFviCyhwj3vt","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/report.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Handover — 2026-05-20\\\\n\\\\n> 由 Agent 生成，每次状态变更后自动更新。硬限 150 行。\\\\n\\\\n## 运行中\\\\n| exp_id | 假设 | 状态 | 关键指标 | W&B |\\\\n|--------|------|------|---------|-----|\\\\n| exp-item-alignment-check | Open LLM Leaderboard v1 per-item responses share the same deterministic item ordering as PSN-IRT combine.csv (both generated by lm-eval-harness), enabling direct positional alignment of v1 response vectors with PSN-IRT 4PL item parameters without content-based matching | — | — | — |\\\\n\\\\n## 待处理\\\\n- exp-power-theory: Detection power of lz* follows an analytic function of n_items and contamination level derivable from Snijders (2001) variance formula, and this theoretical curve explains the empirically observed inverted-U shape and n_items dependence with R²>0.95 against simulation data（准备中）\\\\n\\\\n## 近期结论\\\\n- **exp-empirical-null** (negative): Bootstrap empirical null of lz* under 4PL model shows systematic positive bias (mean>>0) and inflated variance (std>>1) for real LLM response data, quantifying the degree to which LLMs violate IRT local independence/unidimensionality assumptions — this bias explains why 95% of cells are flagged with absolute thresholds ← 基于 exp-two-sided\\\\n  [Empirical Null Q-Q Plots](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/exp-empirical-null/chart/qq_plots_by_benchmark.png) | [Empirical Null Distributions](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/exp-empirical-null/chart/null_distributions.png) | [KS Test Results](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/exp-empirical-null/data/ks_test_results.csv) | [Null Bias Table](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/exp-empirical-null/data/null_bias_table.csv) | [Unflagged Cells Analysis](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/exp-empirical-null/report/unflagged_analysis.md) | [Empirical Null Summary](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/exp-empirical-null/data/empirical_null_summary.json)\\\\n- **exp-leaderboard-data-recon** (success): Open LLM Leaderboard v1 results repo on HuggingFace contains per-item binary response logs (not just aggregate scores) for a substantial number of models, enabling large-scale person-fit analysis without running inference ourselves\\\\n  [Leaderboard Data Recon Report](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/exp-leaderboard-data-recon/report/report.md)\\\\n- **exp-extended-sim** (success): Extended simulation with finer contamination levels (60/75/90%) and fixed 100% NaN handling will reveal the precise dual-regime crossover point where lz* flips from negative (aberrant) to positive (over-consistent), and inverted-U power curve shape is confirmed across all benchmarks ← 基于 sim_001\\\\n\\\\n## 趋势\\\\n成功 3 / 负向 3 / 失败 0 / 共 6\\\\n\\\\n## 下一步\\\\n（无活跃 idea，请通过 ideas.md 添加）\\\\n\\\\n## 资源状态\\\\nbjb2-36806: 无 GPU 信息\\\\n\\\\n## 告警\\\\n（无）\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2821, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AGWFHzQ6EuiqeeLRTJHdE3","session_id":"89eb5c8b-0721-4f89-9e3a-11c1abe48cca","uuid":"512e59c1-affd-42ca-a952-318e007e2259","timestamp":"2026-05-20T10:18:20.986Z"}
